    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0617" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v15/pg589"/>

                <head>315. Letter From President Eisenhower to Prime Minister Ben Gurion<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d315-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Prime Minister</hi>: I have delayed replying
                    to your important letter to me of March sixteenth<anchor n="2" xml:id="d315-f2"
                    /> because of the rapid developments that have been taking place, including
                    notably the mission of Secretary-General Hammarskjold. We are awaiting his
                    report with hope and confidence.</p>
                <p>The only reply I can give you at this moment to the chief subject of your letter,
                    the question of the sale of armaments, is a straightforward one. You have
                    presented your case forcefully and eloquently. But there are other factors to
                    which you do not allude, factors affecting the ability of the United States to
                    maintain its influence for peace in the area. We are not persuaded that it would
                    serve the cause of peace and stability in the world for the United States now to
                    accede to your request for arms sales. We continue to weigh the matter carefully
                    in the light of developments, and I may have occasion to communicate with you
                        further.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d315-f3"/></p>
                <p>With kindest personal regard and best wishes,</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dwight D. Eisenhower</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
